From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Skia] A composited frame has no depth or stencil buffer

Every buffer the compositor renders into gets a depth and stencil
renderbuffer, which the TextureMapper clips with. Composited with Skia it
goes unused, but a tiled GPU still loads and stores it with every frame:
on the Mali-450, a 1734x1042 frame costs 8.8 ms with one attached and
3.6 ms without. Composited with Skia, attach none; Skia is told there are
no stencil bits and clips without them.

---
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -182,6 +182,11 @@
     glGenFramebuffers(1, &m_fbo);
     glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, m_fbo);
 
+    // Only the TextureMapper clips with the stencil. Skia, told there is none, clips without one, and a
+    // tiled GPU then loads and stores no depth and stencil buffer with every frame.
+    if (m_surface->useSkia())
+        return;
+
     glGenRenderbuffers(1, &m_depthStencilBuffer);
     glBindRenderbuffer(GL_RENDERBUFFER, m_depthStencilBuffer);
     glRenderbufferStorage(GL_RENDERBUFFER, GL_DEPTH24_STENCIL8_OES, size.width(), size.height());
